   "text": {
    "L1": "An arithmetic expression is a sum of terms. We must evaluate each part in the right order.",
    "L2": "First, split an expression at plus and minus signs outside brackets.",
    "L3": "Products and quotients inside each term are worked out before the terms are added or subtracted.",
    "L4": "So 3 plus 4 times 2 is 11, not 14. The multiplication term is worked out first.",
    "L5": "Brackets come first. In 40 minus bracket 12 minus 4 bracket plus 3 times 5, the bracket becomes 8.",
    "L6": "Now the terms are 40, minus 8, and plus 15. Adding them gives 47.",
    "L7": "Terms may be swapped, but each term keeps its own sign. Twenty minus 7 plus 3 can become 20 plus 3 minus 7.",
    "L8": "Now check this expression: 12 plus 3 times 5 minus 8 divided by 2. Choose its value."
   },
